pbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1d6f28ec9038125745b691a7c19ab1a3bbd715565fd904d59b8337435b2032ae","event_uuid":"81927107-bb68-4f2d-a0cb-440eb6273f67","position":{"commit_sha":"1ed88fdc4ca7106ad934e9a27cdc83798351f833","position":"1787123674613092001-81927107-bb68-4f2d-a0cb-440eb6273f67"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4b1ef39093e5a5c0496e07231e3ed0136011956f67ec40bacac09401b5f01fee","event_uuid":"69358411-3ac7-46d7-952e-747b5b9016d9","position":{"commit_sha":"45c644fc7c90a38665424b1c4ff732ea6b382209","position":"1787123710315351001-69358411-3ac7-46d7-952e-747b5b9016d9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed via Gerrit change 1895 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 on the docs-only route), rebased+submitted as 4d1d2d3a. Rewrote the two stale transition/claim --force passages (AGENTS.md start-work-gate paragraph + docs/user-guide.md claim paragraph) to the force-everywhere + absent-attestation + CI-certification model per the 2026-08-18 ruling. MCP docstrings were already corrected by scratchy-leprous-galago. Out-of-scope CLI-only families (--allow-secret-pattern, bridge setup) left unchanged.","timestamp":1787123710315351001}],"created_at":1787080938893507001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"29bc8442-54d0-4fae-9503-b61a9b4fcfd7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"},{"link_uuid":"aa2f3787-25e5-48a7-9e12-2e69f0de3acd","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1128-505b-54ac-497f"},{"link_uuid":"b1a17002-2b20-4e4a-9109-c37258140d0d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6bb5-6392-52e6-421d"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe 2026-08-18 operator ruling (signed, recorded on restoring-shallow-blobfish)\nrescinded the older \"force is CLI/library-only\" policy: `--force[=<reason>]` is now\nallowed through EVERY command surface — library, CLI, and MCP. Auditability no longer\ncomes from withholding the capability from MCP; it comes from the ABSENCE of a signed\nattestation. A forced write produces no certification, and projects that want to prevent\nforce from circumventing a gate check for that certification in their CI pipeline.\n\nThe MCP-parity sibling (scratchy-leprous-galago, landed) already exposes reason-bearing\n`force: str | None` on `transition_ticket` and `claim_ticket` and rewrote the tool\ndocstrings to the absent-attestation model. The canonical prose has NOT caught up: two\ndocuments still assert force is CLI-only / not exposed over MCP for the transition+claim\nsurface, contradicting the shipped code. This is a docs-only correction.\n\n## Approach\n\nRewrite the stale transition/claim `--force` prose to the ruling's model in place, without\ntouching code or the already-correct MCP docstrings:\n\n1. AGENTS.md: the start-work-gate `--force[=<reason>]` paragraph ends \"it is CLI-only and\n   not exposed over MCP.\" Replace that clause with the force-everywhere + absent-attestation\n   + CI-certification-enforcement model. Because the Copilot and Claude bridge files import\n   AGENTS.md, this single edit propagates to every harness.\n2. docs/user-guide.md: the `rebar claim <id> --force[=<reason>]` paragraph ends \"`--force`\n   is CLI-only: it is not exposed over MCP (an MCP client always goes through the configured\n   gate).\" Replace with the same force-everywhere + absent-attestation model.\n\nThe edits are scoped strictly to the transition+claim `--force` blast radius named in the\nruling. Unrelated CLI-only statements about OTHER bypass families stay untouched: the\n`--allow-secret-pattern` secret-scan override paragraph in docs/user-guide.md, the\ninteractive `bridge setup` wizard, and the release-notes setup-wizard note are all distinct\nconcepts and out of scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- AGENTS.md — rewrite the trailing CLI-only clause of the start-work `--force` paragraph.\n- docs/user-guide.md — rewrite the trailing CLI-only sentence of the claim `--force`\n  paragraph.\n\nNo code, tests, MCP docstrings (already correct), config, or event-schema changes.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only change with no executable behavior, so there is no unit test to add;\nverification is by inspection and repo-wide grep:\n\n- After the edit, `grep -rni \"cli-only\" AGENTS.md docs/user-guide.md` returns no line that\n  claims the transition or claim `--force` is CLI-only or unavailable over MCP (the\n  surviving matches are the out-of-scope secret-pattern / bridge-setup families).\n- `grep -rni \"not exposed over mcp\" AGENTS.md docs/user-guide.md` returns no transition/claim\n  `--force` match.\n- The rewritten passages state force is available on lib/CLI/MCP, that audit comes from the\n  absent signed attestation, and that CI certification-checks are the enforcement lever.\n- `make lint` stays green (prose-only; no code touched).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AGENTS.md states the transition/claim `--force[=<reason>]` override is available on\n      all surfaces (library, CLI, MCP), not CLI-only.\n- [x] docs/user-guide.md states the claim `--force` override is exposed over MCP, not\n      CLI-only.\n- [x] Both rewritten passages describe the absent-signed-attestation audit model and the\n      CI-certification enforcement option.\n- [x] No remaining claim in AGENTS.md or docs/user-guide.md that the transition or claim\n      `--force` is CLI-only / unavailable over MCP.\n- [x] Out-of-scope CLI-only statements (secret-pattern override, bridge setup, release-notes\n      wizard) are left unchanged.\n- [x] The wording is consistent with the shipped MCP surface (scratchy) and the already-\n      updated `_mcp_writes.py` docstrings.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"rewrite the start-work --force CLI-only clause to the force-everywhere/absent-attestation model"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"rewrite the claim --force CLI-only sentence to force-everywhere/absent-attestation"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1128-505b-54ac-497f"],["relates_to","6bb5-6392-52e6-421d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e42b2319-a39c-41a5-a8ec-703fa26e4dd4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d8c1-e75e-77d8-4c00","ticket_type":"task","title":"Docs: force allowed on all surfaces, audited by absent attestation (AGENTS.md + MCP)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0bbed48b-d927-4843-b737-2dc840242540","46c8d389-43ae-45eb-82b0-dfde5c55543f","b9865cfa-b4ba-4c58-9d9e-d98515c40462","9ddc862c-57d9-4a9e-8ad7-a1ad88a369e1","860ddefe-4159-46a5-9c42-429348e63dd3","b1a17002-2b20-4e4a-9109-c37258140d0d","3b8fea30-8898-49c4-8d68-3623d383dd12","ab858ec4-a2ac-4cdd-b255-1c5bc2bcaa03","e42b2319-a39c-41a5-a8ec-703fa26e4dd4","81927107-bb68-4f2d-a0cb-440eb6273f67","69358411-3ac7-46d7-952e-747b5b9016d9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787127857262084001,"uuid":"d43a2a73-a3d7-4a24-a68a-901cb6c2ddbf"}